NetHack is really a great game, far superior to all the commerical
ones, but... how about its direct rivals - ADOM and its sequel, JADE?
I'm afraid ADOM has overtaken NH - I mean, ADOM has a lot of useful
and nasty NPCs, a lot of quests, far more items, and a much more
complicated gameplay - and I think that if we want NH  to return back
at the 1st place, there is just one thing to be added. More dungeons.

I know, since from the beginning NH has always been single-dungeon,
and adding more dungeons would be simply revolutionary in the NH
gamepley, and you may think that rivality between roguelikes may not
be something good, but there aren't much possibilities of expanding
and finding ideas is getting harder and harder - a multidungeon game
would mean more NPCs, more items, harder gameplay, and with the
devteam's unique taking care of minimal details, even if we should
wait some years for a unstable NHMultiDungeon 0.0.0a - at the end
we'll have surely the best game ever.

Actually, the game has a lot of branches connected with the dungeon.
If we disconnected them - creating a dungeons for the most impontant
branches - and maybe creating some branches for those new dungeons
shouldn't be that impossibile - the code already supports something
like that. And the wilderness (or how we would like to call it) should
be randomly created every time - not fixed as ADOM's one is.

I don't mean to offend NetHack; just I thought that if we wanted to
have a great game, we could point on the multidungeon functionality.
What's your opinion?

